  instrument        travelsweep   trial seed 000000000135506d   1214 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `orthoname` says this creature NAMES -- nearest-target
                    0.958 vs matched marginals at 0.389 and 0.542, with
                    contexts on. Its targets were 0.29 log units from rest.
                    The shipped vowels are 0.89 apart. Where does it stop?
  the measure       DELIVERED SEPARATION, log(f1|word 1) - log(f1|word 0),
                    against the separation demanded. NOT the nearest-target
                    fraction: these targets are symmetric about rest, so that
                    fraction is a SIGN TEST and is nearly invariant to how far
                    apart they sit. It is reported to show exactly that.
  the ladder        0.29 / 0.58 / 0.89 / 1.20 log units on F1, F2 pinned.
                    0.58 reproduces `orthoname`'s `collide` bit-for-bit;
                    0.89 is the shipped vowel pair's own F1 separation.
  the control       matched marginal at EVERY rung: same targets, same reward
                    rate, conditionality removed. Its delivered separation
                    should be zero, since a word-blind target averages to rest.
  the prediction    `transfer-curve` and `ctxbias` agree on a ~234 Hz
                    asymptote, which is +0.32 / -0.47 log units from rest. If
                    that governs here the curve BENDS inside this ladder.
  the refusal       if the 0.29 rung does not beat its own control at 2 SE
                    the instrument is dead and the curve is not read. 36 seeds.

